  "verdict_hot": "Not exceeded: the hottest capsule hour of 30 ERA5 years is 62.9 °C (sunlit, α 0.95, still air, adiabatic base; 2010-08-08T13:00, air 37.4 °C) against the 70 °C EDLC rating — margin 7.1 K; 52.0 °C at α 0.5; shaded (open-sky diffuse only) 48.9 °C. With still-air h_c × 0.7 (the correlation off its home geometry) the sunlit worst is 66.4 °C — margin 3.6 K (the h_c shift alone is 3.5 K), so for a DARK finish in full sun the margin is of the order of the model's own uncertainty, while a light one keeps ≥ 16.0 K. The capsule requirement's upper 85 °C is not approached in this climate. NOT modelled and moving the hot answer UP: sunlit bark conducting through the flange rim; ERA5 smoothing of station maxima.",
  "verdict_aging": "The EDLC ages at T_eff 13.0 °C in open air (vendor 2×/10 K over 262992 hours), not at the 10 °C reference point; under the radome 14.3–17.3 °C shaded and 17.3–26.5 °C sunlit. At the ratified VBAT_OV the life is 19.1–62.0 yr in air and 7.5–62.0 yr across every case: the conservative voltage coefficient stays BELOW 20 yr in every case, the optimistic one stays ABOVE 20 yr in every case — so the 20-year claim now rests on the vendor voltage coefficient alone."
